  "model_rules": [
    "Treaty effective dates date a legal framework, not the origin of a Nation or its governance.",
    "First Nations governments have their own citizens, institutions and accountability arrangements; place them as governments, linked by agreements, not beneath a provincial ministry.",
    "Do not derive Indigenous governmental legitimacy from eligibility to vote in a provincial election.",
    "Financial agreements, service agreements, regional-district membership and hospital-district membership are separate relationships.",
    "The latest Kitselas/Kitsumkalum governance facts describe regional-hospital-district membership even where a Nation does not join the regional district; do not merge those two memberships."
  ],
  "remaining": "An exhaustive inventory of every First Nation’s constitution, council, delegation, service agreement and historical treaty relationship is outside the completed named-agreement set. Detailed boundary/member-government changes and all later treaty amendments require separate dated records."
}
